# Cloudflare Pages custom response headers.
#
# The seven reference PDFs are course collateral — the job aids a learner
# downloads while working through the modules — not portfolio pieces meant
# to be found cold in a search result. A PDF has no <head>, so there is no
# meta tag to mark them with; the only way to keep them out of the index is
# this response header.
#
# Two things follow from that, and both matter if anyone edits the crawl
# config later:
#
#   1. These paths are deliberately NOT in sitemap.xml. Submitting a URL
#      that is also marked noindex earns a "Submitted URL marked 'noindex'"
#      error in Search Console — it would trade the buckets we are clearing
#      for a new one.
#   2. robots.txt deliberately does NOT disallow /reference/. A disallowed
#      path is never fetched, so Googlebot would never see the header below
#      and the URLs could still surface as bare links. Crawlable-but-noindex
#      is the combination that actually removes them.
#
# The needs-analysis, evaluation and build PDFs are the behind-the-build
# portfolio work and stay indexable — they are the only crawlable form of
# that content, since the app is hash-routed and its artifact pages sit
# behind fragments Google ignores.

/reference/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
